#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2836
msgid ""
"Check for leaked memory in autorelease pools that will never be drained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2840
msgid "osx.cocoa.SelfInit (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2842
msgid "Check that 'self' is properly initialized inside an initializer method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2874
msgid "osx.cocoa.SuperDealloc (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2876
msgid "Warn about improper use of '[super dealloc]' in Objective-C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2894
msgid "osx.cocoa.UnusedIvars (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2896
msgid "Warn about private ivars that are never used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2911
msgid "osx.cocoa.VariadicMethodTypes (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2913
msgid ""
"Check for passing non-Objective-C types to variadic collection "
"initialization methods that expect only Objective-C types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2925
msgid "osx.coreFoundation.CFError (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2927
msgid "Check usage of `CFErrorRef *` parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2943
msgid "osx.coreFoundation.CFNumber (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2945
msgid "Check for proper uses of CFNumber APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2956
msgid "osx.coreFoundation.CFRetainRelease (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2958
msgid "Check for null arguments to CFRetain/CFRelease/CFMakeCollectable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2976
msgid "osx.coreFoundation.containers.OutOfBounds (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2978
msgid "Checks for index out-of-bounds when using 'CFArray' API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2989
msgid "osx.coreFoundation.containers.PointerSizedValues (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:2991
msgid ""
"Warns if 'CFArray', 'CFDictionary', 'CFSet' are created with non-pointer-"
"size values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3001
msgid "Fuchsia"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3003
msgid ""
"Fuchsia is an open source capability-based operating system currently being "
"developed by Google. This section describes checkers that can find various "
"misuses of Fuchsia APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3009
msgid "fuchsia.HandleChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3011
msgid ""
"Handles identify resources. Similar to pointers they can be leaked, double "
"freed, or use after freed. This check attempts to find such problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3025
msgid "WebKit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3027
msgid ""
"WebKit is an open-source web browser engine available for macOS, iOS and "
"Linux. This section describes checkers that can find issues in WebKit "
"codebase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3030
msgid ""
"Most of the checkers focus on memory management for which WebKit uses custom "
"implementation of reference counted smartpointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3032
msgid "Checkers are formulated in terms related to ref-counting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3033
msgid "*Ref-counted type* is either `Ref<T>` or `RefPtr<T>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3034
msgid ""
"*Ref-countable type* is any type that implements `ref()` and `deref()` "
"methods as `RefPtr<>` is a template (i. e. relies on duck typing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3035
msgid "*Uncounted type* is ref-countable but not ref-counted type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3039
msgid "webkit.RefCntblBaseVirtualDtor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3041
msgid ""
"All uncounted types used as base classes must have a virtual destructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3043
msgid ""
"Ref-counted types hold their ref-countable data by a raw pointer and allow "
"implicit upcasting from ref-counted pointer to derived type to ref-counted "
"pointer to base type. This might lead to an object of (dynamic) derived type "
"being deleted via pointer to the base class type which C++ standard defines "
"as UB in case the base class doesn't have virtual destructor `[expr.delete]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3056
msgid "webkit.NoUncountedMemberChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3058
msgid ""
"Raw pointers and references to uncounted types can't be used as class "
"members. Only ref-counted types are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3075
msgid "webkit.UncountedLambdaCapturesChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3077
msgid ""
"Raw pointers and references to uncounted types can't be captured in lambdas. "
"Only ref-counted types are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3094
msgid "Experimental Checkers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3096
msgid ""
"*These are checkers with known issues or limitations that keep them from "
"being on by default. They are likely to have false positives. Bug reports "
"and especially patches are welcome.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3098
msgid "alpha.clone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3102
msgid "alpha.clone.CloneChecker (C, C++, ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3104
msgid "Reports similar pieces of code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3124
msgid "alpha.core"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3128
msgid "alpha.core.BoolAssignment (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3130
msgid "Warn about assigning non-{0,1} values to boolean variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3140
msgid "alpha.core.C11Lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3142
msgid ""
"Similarly to {ref}`alpha.unix.PthreadLock <alpha-unix-PthreadLock>`, checks "
"for the locking/unlocking of `mtx_t` mutexes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3157
msgid "alpha.core.CastToStruct (C, C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3159
msgid "Check for cast from non-struct pointer to struct pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3179
msgid "alpha.core.Conversion (C, C++, ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3181
msgid "Loss of sign/precision in implicit conversions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3203
msgid "alpha.core.DanglingPtrDeref (C, C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3205
msgid ""
"Check for dereferences of pointers that refer to an object whose lifetime "
"has already ended. Such a pointer is dangling. The checker reports it when "
"it is dereferenced and when it is passed to a function. A return statement "
"that does not dereference the pointer does not lead to a report. Such a case "
"is reported by the {ref}`core-StackAddressEscape` checker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3211
msgid ""
"Each object is reported at most once on an execution path. If the same "
"dangling pointer is used several times then only the first use is reported. "
"Setting the pointer to null when the object goes out of scope avoids the "
"dangling pointer and suppresses the report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3235
msgid ""
"The `-analyzer-config cfg-lifetime=true` option is a prerequisite for these "
"reports. Without it the checker does not report anything and no error is "
"emitted by the analyzer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3241
msgid ""
"If the analyzer cannot analyze the body of the called function, for example "
"because its definition is not available in the given translation unit, then "
"a dangling pointer passed to it is reported even if the function would never "
"dereference it. This can lead to false positives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3263
msgid "alpha.core.DynamicTypeChecker (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3265
msgid ""
"Check for cases where the dynamic and the static type of an object are "
"unrelated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3278
msgid "alpha.core.PointerArithm (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3280
msgid "Check for pointer arithmetic on locations other than array elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3292
msgid "alpha.core.StackAddressAsyncEscape (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3294
msgid ""
"Check that addresses to stack memory do not escape the function that "
"involves dispatch_after or dispatch_async. This checker is a part of `core."
"StackAddressEscape`, but is temporarily disabled until some false positives "
"are fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3316
msgid "alpha.core.StdVariant (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3318
msgid ""
"Check if a value of active type is retrieved from an `std::variant` instance "
"with `std::get`. In case of bad variant type access (the accessed type "
"differs from the active type) a warning is emitted. Currently, this checker "
"does not take exception handling into account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3331
msgid "alpha.core.TestAfterDivZero (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3333
msgid ""
"Check for division by variable that is later compared against 0. Either the "
"comparison is useless or there is division by zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3345
msgid "alpha.core.UseAfterLifetimeEnd (C, C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3347
msgid ""
"Check for returned pointers and references that are bound to an object whose "
"lifetime ends when the function returns. The checker only analyzes code that "
"is annotated with the `[[clang::lifetimebound]]` attribute. The annotation "
"tells the checker which object the returned value is bound to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3361
msgid ""
"The attribute states that the returned value is dangling after the lifetime "
"of the annotated parameter, or of the implicit object argument, has ended. "
"Refer to the [documentation](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AttributeReference."
"html#lifetimebound) of this Clang attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3378
msgid "**Related Checkers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3380
msgid ""
"{ref}`core-stackaddressescape` reports returning the address of a local "
"object directly. This checker extends that detection through functions that "
"are annotated with `[[clang::lifetimebound]]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3384
msgid ""
"{ref}`alpha-core-danglingptrderef` reports use-after-scope errors anywhere "
"in the function and does not rely on annotations. This checker reports the "
"value that is returned from the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3388
msgid ""
"{ref}`cplusplus-innerpointer` reports similar errors for inner pointers of C+"
"+ containers that are used after re/deallocation without relying on "
"annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3404
msgid ""
"The checker trusts the annotation, so any incorrect annotation can cause "
"false positives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3407
msgid ""
"A dangling pointer that is stored in a compound value is never reported "
"regardless of how the value is used. This includes struct fields and arrays "
"of pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3411
msgid ""
"Only objects whose memory region is on the stack are tracked. A returned "
"value that is bound to heap-allocated memory is not reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3416
msgid "alpha.core.StoreToImmutable (C, C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3418
msgid ""
"Check for writes to immutable memory regions. This implements part of SEI "
"CERT Rule ENV30-C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3420
msgid ""
"This checker detects attempts to write to memory regions that are marked as "
"immutable, including const variables, string literals, and other const-"
"qualified memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3429
msgid ""
"Avoid writing to const-qualified memory regions. If you need to modify the "
"data, remove the const qualifier from the original declaration or use a "
"mutable copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3432
msgid "alpha.cplusplus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3436
msgid "alpha.cplusplus.DeleteWithNonVirtualDtor (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3438
msgid ""
"Reports destructions of polymorphic objects with a non-virtual destructor in "
"their base class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3459
msgid "alpha.cplusplus.InvalidatedIterator (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3461
msgid "Check for use of invalidated iterators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3474
msgid "alpha.cplusplus.IteratorRange (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3476
msgid "Check for iterators used outside their valid ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3487
msgid "alpha.cplusplus.MismatchedIterator (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3489
msgid ""
"Check for use of iterators of different containers where iterators of the "
"same container are expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3511
msgid "alpha.cplusplus.SmartPtr (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3513
msgid "Check for dereference of null smart pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3522
msgid "alpha.deadcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3526
msgid "alpha.deadcode.UnreachableCode (C, C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3528
msgid "Check unreachable code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3556
msgid "alpha.fuchsia"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3560
msgid "alpha.fuchsia.Lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3562
msgid ""
"Similarly to {ref}`alpha.unix.PthreadLock <alpha-unix-PthreadLock>`, checks "
"for the locking/unlocking of fuchsia mutexes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3575
msgid "alpha.llvm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3579
msgid "alpha.llvm.Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3581
msgid "Check code for LLVM codebase conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3583
msgid ""
"A StringRef should not be bound to a temporary std::string whose lifetime is "
"shorter than the StringRef's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3584
msgid "Clang AST nodes should not have fields that can allocate memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3586
msgid "alpha.osx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3590
msgid "alpha.osx.cocoa.DirectIvarAssignment (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3592
msgid "Check for direct assignments to instance variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3609
msgid "alpha.osx.cocoa.DirectIvarAssignmentForAnnotatedFunctions (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3611
msgid ""
"Check for direct assignments to instance variables in the methods annotated "
"with `objc_no_direct_instance_variable_assignment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3634
msgid "alpha.osx.cocoa.InstanceVariableInvalidation (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3636
msgid ""
"Check that the invalidatable instance variables are invalidated in the "
"methods annotated with objc_instance_variable_invalidator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3662
msgid "alpha.osx.cocoa.MissingInvalidationMethod (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3664
msgid ""
"Check that the invalidation methods are present in classes that contain "
"invalidatable instance variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3686
msgid "alpha.osx.cocoa.localizability.PluralMisuseChecker (ObjC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3688
msgid ""
"Warns against using one vs. many plural pattern in code when generating "
"localized strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3708
msgid "alpha.security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3712
msgid "alpha.security.ReturnPtrRange (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3714
msgid "Check for an out-of-bound pointer being returned to callers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3730
msgid "alpha.unix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3734
msgid "alpha.unix.PthreadLock (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3736
msgid ""
"Simple lock -> unlock checker. Applies to: `pthread_mutex_lock, "
"pthread_rwlock_rdlock, pthread_rwlock_wrlock, lck_mtx_lock, "
"lck_rw_lock_exclusive` `lck_rw_lock_shared, pthread_mutex_trylock, "
"pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock, pthread_rwlock_tryrwlock, lck_mtx_try_lock, "
"lck_rw_try_lock_exclusive, lck_rw_try_lock_shared, pthread_mutex_unlock, "
"pthread_rwlock_unlock, lck_mtx_unlock, lck_rw_done`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3743
msgid ""
"`WarnOnLockOrderReversal` (boolean). If set to true, the checker will warn "
"on non-LIFO unlock order (possible lock order reversal). Defaults to false "
"because detecting real lock order violations requires cross-path analysis of "
"acquisition order, which the analyzer's single-path engine does not support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3782
msgid "alpha.unix.SimpleStream (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3784
msgid ""
"Check for misuses of stream APIs. Check for misuses of stream APIs: `fopen, "
"fclose` (demo checker, the subject of the demo ([Slides](https://llvm.org/"
"devmtg/2012-11/Zaks-Rose-Checker24Hours.pdf) , [Video](https://youtu.be/"
"kdxlsP5QVPw)) by Anna Zaks and Jordan Rose presented at the [2012 LLVM "
"Developers' Meeting](https://llvm.org/devmtg/2012-11/))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3806
msgid "alpha.unix.cstring.BufferOverlap (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3808
msgid ""
"Checks for overlap in two buffer arguments. Applies to: `memcpy, mempcpy, "
"wmemcpy, wmempcpy`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3819
msgid "alpha.unix.cstring.OutOfBounds (C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3821
msgid ""
"Check for out-of-bounds access in string functions, such as: `memcpy, bcopy, "
"strcpy, strncpy, strcat, strncat, memmove, memcmp, memset` and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3824
msgid ""
"This check also works with string literals, except there is a known bug in "
"that the analyzer cannot detect embedded NULL characters when determining "
"the string length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3841
msgid "alpha.WebKit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3843
msgid "alpha.webkit.ForwardDeclChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3845
msgid ""
"Check for local variables, member variables, and function arguments that are "
"forward declared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3863
msgid "alpha.webkit.MemoryUnsafeCastChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3865
msgid ""
"Check for all casts from a base type to its derived type as these might be "
"memory-unsafe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3867
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3878
msgid ""
"For all cast operations (C-style casts, static_cast, reinterpret_cast, "
"dynamic_cast), if the source type a `Base*` and the destination type is "
"`Derived*`, where `Derived` inherits from `Base`, the static analyzer should "
"signal an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3880
msgid "This applies to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3882
msgid ""
"C structs, C++ structs and classes, and Objective-C classes and protocols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3883
msgid "Pointers and references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3884
msgid ""
"Inside template instantiations and macro expansions that are visible to the "
"compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3886
msgid ""
"For types like this, instead of using built in casts, the programmer will "
"use helper functions that internally perform the appropriate type check and "
"disable static analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3888
msgid "alpha.webkit.NoDeleteChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3890
msgid ""
"Check that `[[clang::annotate_type(\"webkit.nodelete\")]]` annotation does "
"not appear on a function which could delete an object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3902
msgid ""
"`[[clang::annotate_type(\"webkit.nodelete\")]]` annotation makes the "
"function ignored for the purpose of other WebKit smart pointer checkers. For "
"example, `alpha.webkit.UncountedCallArgsChecker` will ignore a function call "
"with this annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3905
msgid "alpha.webkit.NoUncheckedPtrMemberChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3907
msgid ""
"Raw pointers and references to an object which supports CheckedPtr or "
"CheckedRef can't be used as class members. Only CheckedPtr, CheckedRef, "
"RefPtr, or Ref are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3922 ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3936
msgid ""
"See [WebKit Guidelines for Safer C++ Programming](https://github.com/WebKit/"
"WebKit/wiki/Safer-CPP-Guidelines) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3924
msgid "alpha.webkit.NoUnretainedMemberChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3926
msgid ""
"Raw pointers and references to a NS or CF object can't be used as class "
"members or ivars. Only RetainPtr is allowed for CF types regardless of "
"whether ARC is enabled or disabled. Only RetainPtr or OSObjectPtr is allowed "
"for NS types when ARC is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3938
msgid "alpha.webkit.UnretainedLambdaCapturesChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3940
msgid ""
"Raw pointers and references to NS or CF types can't be captured in lambdas. "
"Only RetainPtr is allowed for CF types regardless of whether ARC is enabled "
"or disabled, and only RetainPtr or OSObjectPtr is allowed for NS types when "
"ARC is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3953
msgid "alpha.webkit.UncountedCallArgsChecker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3955
msgid ""
"The goal of this rule is to make sure that lifetime of any dynamically "
"allocated ref-countable object passed as a call argument spans past the end "
"of the call. This applies to call to any function, method, lambda, function "
"pointer or functor. Ref-countable types aren't supposed to be allocated on "
"stack so we check arguments for parameters of raw pointers and references to "
"uncounted types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3957
msgid ""
"Here are some examples of situations that we warn about as they *might* be "
"potentially unsafe. The logic is that either we're able to guarantee that an "
"argument is safe or it's considered if not a bug then bug-prone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3975
msgid ""
"Although we are enforcing member variables to be ref-counted by `webkit."
"NoUncountedMemberChecker` any method of the same class still has "
"unrestricted access to these. Since from a caller's perspective we can't "
"guarantee a particular member won't get modified by callee (directly or "
"indirectly) we don't consider values obtained from members safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3977
msgid ""
"Note: It's likely this heuristic could be made more precise with fewer false "
"positives - for example calls to free functions that don't have any "
"parameter other than the pointer should be safe as the callee won't be able "
"to tamper with the member unless it's a global variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3989
msgid ""
"The implementation of this rule is a heuristic - we define a whitelist of "
"kinds of values that are considered safe to be passed as arguments. If we "
"can't prove an argument is safe it's considered an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3991
msgid "Allowed kinds of arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:3993
msgid ""
"values obtained from ref-counted objects (including temporaries as those "
"survive the call too)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4006
msgid "forwarding uncounted arguments from caller to callee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4014
msgid "Caller of `foo()` is responsible for `a`'s lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4016
msgid "`this` pointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4024
msgid ""
"Caller of `foo()` is responsible for keeping the memory pointed to by `this` "
"pointer safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4026
msgid "constants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/checkers.md:4032
msgid ""
"We also define a set of safe transformations which if passed a safe value as "
"an input provide (usually it's the return value) a safe value (or an object "
"that provides safe values). This is also a heuristic."
msgstr ""

